{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# ML-08 — Capstone Modeling Lane\n\n[![Open In Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg)](https://colab.research.google.com/github/Di-pesh/flyinterm/blob/main/work/notebooks/w05_model.ipynb)\n\n## 1. Method choice and why\n\nI am using a transparent logistic-regression model with client-group validation. This is the right choice for this lane because the dataset is structured, interpretable, and the objective is a ranking/triage decision rather than a large-scale deep-learning problem. Logistic regression is easy to explain to content stakeholders, it works well with mixed numeric and categorical inputs, and it gives a probability score that can be used to order the refresh queue.\n\nThe model is useful because we can inspect which features drive risk and explain recommendations in plain language.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "root = Path.cwd().resolve()\n",
    "processed = None\n",
    "for p in [root, *root.parents]:\n",
    "    candidate = p / 'data' / 'processed' / 'refresh_feature_vector.csv'\n",
    "    if candidate.exists():\n",
    "        processed = candidate\n",
    "        break\n",
    "if processed is None:\n",
    "    subprocess.run([sys.executable, 'scripts/01_prepare_features.py'], check=True)\n",
    "    processed = root / 'data' / 'processed' / 'refresh_feature_vector.csv'\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(processed)\n",
    "print(f'Prepared rows: {len(df):,}')\n",
    "print(f'Positive rate: {df[\'is_declining_label\'].mean():.3f}')\n",
    "print(df[['client_id', 'content_id', 'is_declining_label', 'impressions_90d', 'avg_position']].head().to_string(index=False))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 2. Split design\n\nThe honest split is a grouped client holdout: rows from the same client stay in the same fold so the model does not memorize a client’s pattern and then look artificially strong on similar pages. This is more realistic for deployment, because the model is judged on new client conditions rather than on pages it has already seen from the same client.\n\nI also report the random split as a comparison point, because the gap between random and grouped validation is itself a sign of memorization.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import GroupKFold\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(processed)\n",
    "groups = df['client_id']\n",
    "y = df['is_declining_label']\n",
    "gkf = GroupKFold(n_splits=5)\n",
    "folds = list(gkf.split(df, y, groups))\n",
    "print(f'Number of folds: {len(folds)}')\n",
    "for i, (train_idx, test_idx) in enumerate(folds[:2], start=1):\n",
    "    print(f'Fold {i}: train={len(train_idx):,}, test={len(test_idx):,}, unique clients={df.iloc[test_idx][\'client_id\'].nunique():,}')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 3. Train + compare vs my baseline\n\nThe model is trained on the same feature set and the same outcome definition as the baseline work, but the split is honest. The comparison below uses a naive baseline: predict the majority class and compare it with the model score on the held-out client fold.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score, average_precision_score\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import GroupKFold\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(processed)\n",
    "target = 'is_declining_label'\n",
    "numeric = ['search_volume', 'competition', 'cpc', 'word_count', 'char_count', 'log_impressions_90d', 'log_clicks_90d', 'log_sessions_90d', 'log_ai_sessions_90d', 'days_with_impressions', 'days_with_sessions', 'content_age_days', 'days_since_last_update', 'ctr', 'avg_position', 'engagement_rate', 'scroll_rate', 'ai_traffic_pct']\n",
    "categorical = ['competition_level', 'content_type', 'main_intent', 'age_tier', 'freshness_tier', 'word_count_tier', 'impression_tier', 'position_tier']\n",
    "features = [c for c in numeric + categorical if c in df.columns]\n",
    "X = df[features]\n",
    "y = df[target].astype(int)\n",
    "groups = df['client_id']\n",
    "\n",
    "pre = ColumnTransformer(\n",
    "    transformers=[\n",
    "        ('num', SimpleImputer(strategy='median'), [c for c in numeric if c in X.columns]),\n",
    "        ('cat', Pipeline([('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='most_frequent')), ('ohe', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore'))]), [c for c in categorical if c in X.columns]),\n",
    "    ]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model = Pipeline([('pre', pre), ('lr', LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, class_weight='balanced'))])\n",
    "gkf = GroupKFold(n_splits=3)\n",
    "scores = []\n",
    "for train_idx, test_idx in gkf.split(X, y, groups):\n",
    "    model.fit(X.iloc[train_idx], y.iloc[train_idx])\n",
    "    prob = model.predict_proba(X.iloc[test_idx])[:, 1]\n",
    "    score = roc_auc_score(y.iloc[test_idx], prob)\n",
    "    scores.append(score)\n",
    "\n",
    "baseline = y.mean()\n",
    "print(f'Grouped-fold ROC-AUC across folds: {scores}')\n",
    "print(f'Mean grouped-fold ROC-AUC: {np.mean(scores):.3f}')\n",
    "print(f'Majority-class baseline rate: {baseline:.3f}')\n",
    "print('Interpretation: the model should outperform the majority-rate baseline and do so under a client-grouped holdout.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 4. Errors and interpretation\n\nThe model should be inspected for where it is wrong. A common pattern is that it overweights traffic-level variables and underweights content freshness or content-type nuance. The right next step is to examine false positives and false negatives by client, content type, or position tier. This is more productive than simply chasing a slightly higher metric number.\n\nGood model interpretation asks: which pages does the model rank too highly, which pages does it miss, and what kind of pages are at the edge of the queue?\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import GroupKFold\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(processed)\n",
    "numeric = ['search_volume', 'competition', 'cpc', 'word_count', 'char_count', 'log_impressions_90d', 'log_clicks_90d', 'log_sessions_90d', 'log_ai_sessions_90d', 'days_with_impressions', 'days_with_sessions', 'content_age_days', 'days_since_last_update', 'ctr', 'avg_position', 'engagement_rate', 'scroll_rate', 'ai_traffic_pct']\n",
    "categorical = ['competition_level', 'content_type', 'main_intent', 'age_tier', 'freshness_tier', 'word_count_tier', 'impression_tier', 'position_tier']\n",
    "X = df[[c for c in numeric + categorical if c in df.columns]]\n",
    "y = df['is_declining_label'].astype(int)\n",
    "groups = df['client_id']\n",
    "\n",
    "pre = ColumnTransformer([\n",
    "    ('num', SimpleImputer(strategy='median'), [c for c in numeric if c in X.columns]),\n",
    "    ('cat', Pipeline([('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='most_frequent')), ('ohe', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore'))]), [c for c in categorical if c in X.columns]),\n",
    "])\n",
    "model = Pipeline([('pre', pre), ('lr', LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, class_weight='balanced'))])\n",
    "gkf = GroupKFold(n_splits=3)\n",
    "for fold_idx, (train_idx, test_idx) in enumerate(gkf.split(X, y, groups), start=1):\n",
    "    model.fit(X.iloc[train_idx], y.iloc[train_idx])\n",
    "    prob = model.predict_proba(X.iloc[test_idx])[:, 1]\n",
    "    result = X.iloc[test_idx].copy()\n",
    "    result['actual'] = y.iloc[test_idx].values\n",
    "    result['score'] = prob\n",
    "    result['pred'] = (prob >= 0.5).astype(int)\n",
    "    false_pos = result[(result['actual'] == 0) & (result['pred'] == 1)].sort_values('score', ascending=False).head(5)\n",
    "    false_neg = result[(result['actual'] == 1) & (result['pred'] == 0)].sort_values('score', ascending=True).head(5)\n",
    "    print(f'Fold {fold_idx} error review:')\n",
    "    print('False positives head:')\n",
    "    print(false_pos[['score', 'actual', 'pred']].head().to_string(index=False))\n",
    "    print('False negatives head:')\n",
    "    print(false_neg[['score', 'actual', 'pred']].head().to_string(index=False))\n",
    "    print('---')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## Self-check\n\n- [x] The method and split choice are explicitly justified.\n- [x] The model is compared to a baseline under a grouped validation scheme.\n- [x] Error analysis is included rather than just a metric table.\n- [x] The notebook documents that the model is decision-support and not causal proof.\n"
  }
